{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"The NovaSeq X control software is on a much faster release cadence, and the 5B and 1.5B-600-cycle flow cells shipped only on the X.","detail":"X Series suite releases: v1.1.0 (Jun 27 2023), v1.2.0 (Nov 2 2023), v1.2.2 (May 13 2024), v1.3.0 (Dec 2 2024), v1.3.1 (Jun 23 2025), v1.4.0 (page date Jul 28 2026, while search snippets show release notes effective 19 Mar 2026). That is 6 releases in about 37 months, roughly one every 6 months. The 6000 had 1 release over the same stretch (Jul 2023 to Aug 2026). Search snippets say v1.4.0 adds the 5B flow cell, a 1.5B 600-cycle option, staggered-start scheduling and automatic index detection. Nothing comparable is listed for the 6000, so engineering effort and new features sit on the X.","url":"https://emea.support.illumina.com/sequencing/sequencing_instruments/novaseq-x-novaseq-x-plus/documentation.html","date":"2026-07-28","source_name":"Illumina support, NovaSeq X documentation","source_type":"archive","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"First dated software-cadence comparison of the 6000 vs the X; the 5B flow cell is known, but not that its software launched only on the X."},
